  "notes": "USAGE: イラつく is a casual, colloquial verb meaning to become irritated or annoyed. It is derived from the mimetic イライラ and is common in everyday speech and informal writing.\n\nCONJUGATION: A godan verb — イラつく → イラついた (past), イラつかない (negative), イラついて (te-form).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- イライラ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to be irritated — the standard, slightly less blunt equivalent\n- ⟦むかつく→ムカつく：06357_mukatsuku⟧: to be pissed off — stronger; can also mean to feel nauseous",
